8@P3: hx\nL559@P3: 2\nL560@P3: i =\nL561@P3: 2Dts\nL562@P3: α(2 − α)\nL563@P3: . (17)\nL564@P3: For α\nL565@P3:  1, the variance is Dts/α, which is the value\nL566@P3: expected by a “naive” application of the equipartition\nL567@P3: principle: substituting α = tsk/γ and D = kBT /γ gives\nL568@P3: hx\nL569@P3: 2\nL570@P3: i = kBT /k. However, the variance at finite α is always\nL571@P3: larger and diverges at α\nL572@P3: ∗ = 2, beyond which the motion is\nL573@P3: unstable. Physically, the extra variance comes from over\u0002correcting perturbations. At α = 2, the motion oscillates\nL574@P3: from one side of equilibrium to the other.\nL575@P3: Repeating the argument for unit delay, td = ts, we have\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0608415)\nciteturn15view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0608415\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 474\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://arxiv.org/pdf/1809.02896)\nciteturn15view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 5; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1809.02896\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 471\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn15view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-021-81094-x\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n"
